{"step_index":741,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:37:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-13T21:37:01+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-13T21:37:01+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/codekids/src/lib/speech.ts`\nTotal Lines: 118\nTotal Bytes: 2796\nShowing lines 1 to 118\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"use client\";\n2: \n3: // Web Speech API text-to-speech helper for Bibi AI (FR-AI-06).\n4: // Allows children with emerging literacy to hear Bibi's guidance out loud.\n5: \n6: import { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\n7: \n8: export function isSpeechSupported(): boolean {\n9:   return typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"speechSynthesis\" in window;\n10: }\n11: \n12: /**\n13:  * React hook to safely check speech synthesis support without SSR hydration mismatch.\n14:  */\n15: export function useSpeechSupported(): boolean {\n16:   const [supported, setSupported] = useState(false);\n17: \n18:   useEffect(() => {\n19:     setSupported(isSpeechSupported());\n20:   }, []);\n21: \n22:   return supported;\n23: }\n24: \n25: export function cleanTextForSpeech(text: string): string {\n26:   return text\n27:     // Remove markdown formatting\n28:     .replace(/[*_#`~>]/g, \"\")\n29:     // Remove URLs\n30:     .replace(/https?:\\/\\/\\S+/g, \"\")\n31:     // Remove emojis so the speech engine doesn't read out emoji descriptions\n32:     .replace(/[\\u{1F300}-\\u{1F9FF}\\u{1FA00}-\\u{1FAFF}\\u{2600}-\\u{26FF}\\u{2700}-\\u{27BF}]/gu, \"\")\n33:     // Remove leftover symbols and collapse whitespace\n34:     .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n35:     .trim();\n36: }\n37: \n38: let activeUtterance: SpeechSynthesisUtterance | null = null;\n39: \n40: export function stopSpeaking() {\n41:   if (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"speechSynthesis\" in window) {\n42:     try {\n43:       window.speechSynthesis.cancel();\n44:     } catch {\n45:       // Ignore cancel errors\n46:     }\n47:   }\n48:   activeUtterance = null;\n49: }\n50: \n51: export function speakBibiText(\n52:   text: string,\n53:   callbacks?: {\n54:     onStart?: () => void;\n55:     onEnd?: () => void;\n56:     onError?: (err: unknown) => void;\n57:   }\n58: ) {\n59:   if (!isSpeechSupported()) {\n60:     callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n61:     return;\n62:   }\n63: \n64:   stopSpeaking();\n65: \n66:   const cleaned = cleanTextForSpeech(text);\n67:   if (!cleaned) {\n68:     callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n69:     return;\n70:   }\n71: \n72:   const utterance = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(cleaned);\n73:   activeUtterance = utterance;\n74: \n75:   // Mascot voice personality: friendly, cheerful, slightly higher pitch, gentle pacing for kids\n76:   utterance.pitch = 1.15;\n77:   utterance.rate = 0.95;\n78: \n79:   const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();\n80:   const idVoice = voices.find(\n81:     (v) =>\n82:       v.lang.toLowerCase().startsWith(\"id\") ||\n83:       v.lang.toLowerCase().includes(\"id-id\") ||\n84:       v.name.toLowerCase().includes(\"indonesia\")\n85:   );\n86: \n87:   if (idVoice) {\n88:     utterance.voice = idVoice;\n89:     utterance.lang = idVoice.lang;\n90:   } else {\n91:     utterance.lang = \"id-ID\";\n92:   }\n93: \n94:   utterance.onstart = () => {\n95:     callbacks?.onStart?.();\n96:   };\n97: \n98:   utterance.onend = () => {\n99:     if (activeUtterance === utterance) {\n100:       activeUtterance = null;\n101:     }\n102:     callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n103:   };\n104: \n105:   utterance.onerror = (e) => {\n106:     if (activeUtterance === utterance) {\n107:       activeUtterance = null;\n108:     }\n109:     callbacks?.onError?.(e);\n110:   };\n111: \n112:   try {\n113:     window.speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);\n114:   } catch (err) {\n115:     callbacks?.onError?.(err);\n116:   }\n117: }\n118: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":742,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:37:02Z","input_tokens":2318,"cache_read_tokens":173529,"output_tokens":2590,"thinking":"Investigating how the browser selects voices and methods to ensure a female voice are used. Observed that the `window.speechSynthesis.getVoices()` method provides voice information, including a `voice.name` attribute, which seems to contain gender information. Determined that voice names may indicate gender, enabling the selection of a female voice based on the name.\n\n\nDeveloping a function to filter available voices, prioritizing Indonesian voices. Created keyword lists to identify female and avoid male voices based on `voice.name` and `voice.lang`. The function first attempts to find an explicit female Indonesian voice using these keywords.\n\n\nA fallback strategy prioritizes non-male Indonesian voices if an explicitly female Indonesian voice is unavailable. If no suitable Indonesian voice exists, the function attempts to find any female voice from the available options. Pitch and rate parameters are set to 1.3 and 0.95 respectively, optimizing for a cheerful, clear female voice appropriate for children. To ensure voice availability, `speechSynthesis.onvoiceschanged` will be used to preload voices.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"use client\";\n\n// Web Speech API text-to-speech helper for Bibi AI (FR-AI-06).\n// Allows children with emerging literacy to hear Bibi's guidance out loud in a warm, cheerful female voice.\n\nimport { useState, useEffect } from \"react\";\n\nexport function isSpeechSupported(): boolean {\n  return typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"speechSynthesis\" in window;\n}\n\n/**\n * React hook to safely check speech synthesis support without SSR hydration mismatch.\n */\nexport function useSpeechSupported(): boolean {\n  const [supported, setSupported] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setSupported(isSpeechSupported());\n  }, []);\n\n  return supported;\n}\n\nexport function cleanTextForSpeech(text: string): string {\n  return text\n    // Remove markdown formatting\n    .replace(/[*_#`~>]/g, \"\")\n    // Remove URLs\n    .replace(/https?:\\/\\/\\S+/g, \"\")\n    // Remove emojis so the speech engine doesn't read out emoji descriptions\n    .replace(/[\\u{1F300}-\\u{1F9FF}\\u{1FA00}-\\u{1FAFF}\\u{2600}-\\u{26FF}\\u{2700}-\\u{27BF}]/gu, \"\")\n    // Remove leftover symbols and collapse whitespace\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n    .trim();\n}\n\n/**\n * Specifically finds a female voice, prioritizing Indonesian female voices like\n * \"Microsoft Gadis Online (Natural)\", \"Google Bahasa Indonesia\", \"Damayanti\", \"Siti\".\n */\nexport function getBibiFemaleVoice(): SpeechSynthesisVoice | undefined {\n  if (typeof window === \"undefined\" || !(\"speechSynthesis\" in window)) return undefined;\n\n  const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();\n  if (!voices || voices.length === 0) return undefined;\n\n  // Filter Indonesian voices\n  const idVoices = voices.filter(\n    (v) =>\n      v.lang.toLowerCase().startsWith(\"id\") ||\n      v.lang.toLowerCase().includes(\"id-id\") ||\n      v.name.toLowerCase().includes(\"indonesia\")\n  );\n\n  // Female keywords commonly found in browser voices\n  const femaleKeywords = [\n    \"gadis\",\n    \"female\",\n    \"wanita\",\n    \"perempuan\",\n    \"damayanti\",\n    \"siti\",\n    \"indah\",\n    \"putri\",\n    \"ayu\",\n    \"wulan\",\n    \"lestari\",\n    \"google\", // Google Bahasa Indonesia is a gentle female voice\n  ];\n\n  // Male keywords to filter out\n  const maleKeywords = [\"ardi\", \"male\", \"pria\", \"laki\", \"david\", \"george\", \"guy\"];\n\n  if (idVoices.length > 0) {\n    // 1. Look for explicit female Indonesian voice (e.g. \"Microsoft Gadis\", \"Damayanti\", \"Google Bahasa Indonesia\")\n    const femaleIdVoice = idVoices.find((v) => {\n      const name = v.name.toLowerCase();\n      const isFemale = femaleKeywords.some((k) => name.includes(k));\n      const isMale = maleKeywords.some((k) => name.includes(k));\n      return isFemale && !isMale;\n    });\n    if (femaleIdVoice) return femaleIdVoice;\n\n    // 2. Look for any Indonesian voice that is NOT marked as male\n    const notMaleIdVoice = idVoices.find((v) => {\n      const name = v.name.toLowerCase();\n      return !maleKeywords.some((k) => name.includes(k));\n    });\n    if (notMaleIdVoice) return notMaleIdVoice;\n\n    // 3. Fallback to first available Indonesian voice\n    return idVoices[0];\n  }\n\n  // 4. If no Indonesian voice, try any available female voice\n  const fallbackFemale = voices.find((v) => {\n    const name = v.name.toLowerCase();\n    return femaleKeywords.some((k) => name.includes(k)) && !maleKeywords.some((k) => name.includes(k));\n  });\n\n  return fallbackFemale;\n}\n\nlet activeUtterance: SpeechSynthesisUtterance | null = null;\n\nexport function stopSpeaking() {\n  if (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"speechSynthesis\" in window) {\n    try {\n      window.speechSynthesis.cancel();\n    } catch {\n      // Ignore cancel errors\n    }\n  }\n  activeUtterance = null;\n}\n\nexport function speakBibiText(\n  text: string,\n  callbacks?: {\n    onStart?: () => void;\n    onEnd?: () => void;\n    onError?: (err: unknown) => void;\n  }\n) {\n  if (!isSpeechSupported()) {\n    callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n    return;\n  }\n\n  stopSpeaking();\n\n  const cleaned = cleanTextForSpeech(text);\n  if (!cleaned) {\n    callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const utterance = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(cleaned);\n  activeUtterance = utterance;\n\n  // Mascot persona: Warm, friendly, cheerful female character\n  // Pitch 1.25 - 1.3 gives a bright, feminine, comforting tone for Bibi\n  utterance.pitch = 1.3;\n  utterance.rate = 0.95;\n\n  const femaleVoice = getBibiFemaleVoice();\n  if (femaleVoice) {\n    utterance.voice = femaleVoice;\n    utterance.lang = femaleVoice.lang;\n  } else {\n    utterance.lang = \"id-ID\";\n  }\n\n  utterance.onstart = () => {\n    callbacks?.onStart?.();\n  };\n\n  utterance.onend = () => {\n    if (activeUtterance === utterance) {\n      activeUtterance = null;\n    }\n    callbacks?.onEnd?.();\n  };\n\n  utterance.onerror = (e) => {\n    if (activeUtterance === utterance) {\n      activeUtterance = null;\n    }\n    callbacks?.onError?.(e);\n  };\n\n  try {\n    window.speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);\n  } catch (err) {\n    callbacks?.onError?.(err);\n  }\n}\n","Description":"Update speech.ts to prioritize Indonesian female voices and adjust pitch for feminine mascot persona","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"e:/codekids/src/lib/speech.ts","toolAction":"Updating speech voice selector","toolSummary":"Female voice selector update"}}]}
